From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: stop narrowing cell broadcast on every data call

The connect sequence re-sent SET_BROADCAST_SMS_CONFIG and
SMS_BROADCAST_ACTIVATION on the way to every data call, and the config it
sent named a single range, 4352-4356. The boot configuration has already
sent the full channel set by then, so this narrowed it: on whichever stack
carried data it switched CMAS 4370-4399 back off -- presidential, extreme,
severe and amber alerts -- for the rest of the boot.

Seen on hardware, r61, ch 0xf6:

    4813ms  SET_BROADCAST_SMS_CONFIG  8 ranges   boot configuration
   11271ms  SET_BROADCAST_SMS_CONFIG  1 range    connect sequence

The single-range form does not exist in any capture: across five of them
stock's SET_BROADCAST_SMS_CONFIG carries seven or eight ranges and never
one. Nor does stock tie it to a data call. It sends it one to three times
per stack while configuring the modem -- in two of the five captures
exactly once per stack, which is what is left here -- and a long session
re-sends it later, but always with the full set and never once per context.

Configuring cell broadcast is not part of bringing up a context, so the two
steps are gone. The connect-sequence test pinned them and now records why
they are not there.
--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-client.c
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/mm-sit-client.c
@@ -2785,8 +2785,21 @@
     CONNECT_STEP_DATA_PROFILE,
     CONNECT_STEP_ATTACH_APN,
     CONNECT_STEP_CONFIG_0900,
-    CONNECT_STEP_CONFIG_0106,
-    CONNECT_STEP_CONFIG_0107,
+    /*
+     * Cell broadcast is not part of bringing up a context.
+     *
+     * There were two steps here that re-sent SET_BROADCAST_SMS_CONFIG and
+     * SMS_BROADCAST_ACTIVATION on the way to every data call, and the config
+     * they sent named one range, 4352-4356. The boot configuration has already
+     * sent the full set by then, so this narrowed it: on whichever stack
+     * carried data it switched CMAS 4370-4399 back off -- presidential,
+     * extreme, severe and amber alerts -- for the rest of the boot.
+     *
+     * Stock sends neither here. Across five captures its SET_BROADCAST_SMS_CONFIG
+     * and SMS_BROADCAST_ACTIVATION are always paired, always carry the full
+     * channel set, and always land before the first data call: the last at
+     * 7317ms against a first data call at 10387ms. See mm-sit-boot-config.c.
+     */
     CONNECT_STEP_REGISTRATION,
     CONNECT_STEP_SETUP,
     CONNECT_STEP_FAST_DORMANCY,
@@ -3180,8 +3193,6 @@
                        ConnectContext *ctx,
                        GError        **error)
 {
-    guint8 body_0106[12] = { 0 };
-    guint8 body_0107[8] = { 0 };
     guint8 reserved[4] = { 0 };
 
     switch (ctx->step) {
@@ -3195,16 +3206,6 @@
         return mm_sit_request_new_set_initial_attach_apn (mm_sit_client_next_token (self), ctx->apn, ctx->pdp, &ctx->auth, error);
     case CONNECT_STEP_CONFIG_0900:
         return mm_sit_request_new (0x0900, mm_sit_client_next_token (self), reserved, sizeof (reserved), error);
-    case CONNECT_STEP_CONFIG_0106:
-        body_0106[4] = 0x01;
-        body_0106[6] = 0x11;
-        body_0106[7] = 0x04;
-        body_0106[8] = 0x11;
-        body_0106[10] = 0xff;
-        body_0106[11] = 0x01;
-        return mm_sit_request_new (0x0106, mm_sit_client_next_token (self), body_0106, sizeof (body_0106), error);
-    case CONNECT_STEP_CONFIG_0107:
-        return mm_sit_request_new (0x0107, mm_sit_client_next_token (self), body_0107, sizeof (body_0107), error);
     case CONNECT_STEP_SETUP:
         return mm_sit_request_new_setup_data_call (mm_sit_client_next_token (self), ctx->cid,
                                                    ctx->apn, ctx->pdp, ctx->apn_types, &ctx->auth, error);
--- a/src/plugins/samsung-sit/tests/test-sit-protocol.c
+++ b/src/plugins/samsung-sit/tests/test-sit-protocol.c
@@ -1839,8 +1839,13 @@
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SET_DATA_PROFILE,
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SET_INITIAL_ATTACH_APN,
         0x0900,
-        0x0106,
-        0x0107,
+        /*
+         * No cell broadcast here. Configuring it is not part of bringing up a
+         * context, the boot configuration has already done it with the full
+         * channel set, and what used to be sent here named one range and so
+         * switched CMAS back off on the data stack. Stock sends neither in a
+         * connect sequence.
+         */
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_GET_DATA_REGISTRATION,
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SETUP_DATA_CALL,
         MM_SIT_MESSAGE_SET_FAST_DORMANCY_INFO,
